{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/400636-idigam-and-mankind","id":400636,"title":"Idigam and Mankind.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-10T12:07:40-08:00","id":400636,"title":"Idigam and Mankind.","content":"Could the Idigam have special reactions and &quot;toughts&quot; towards mankind since they are spirit without analog in the physical world and mans are flesh beings without analog in the spiritual world ? (I wonder if it was the case before the death of Father Wolf)<br /> <br /> Since the Idigam are several, maybe one of them is persuaded/wants to be(come) the Spirit of Humanity, Gurdilag is the prood that the Idigam can have this kind of weird toughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T13:04:12-08:00","id":400741,"title":"","content":"Well, the Gamugur likes having humanity worship it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T13:22:59-08:00","id":400785,"title":"","content":"The one time I used an idigam as a primary villain the entity was especially curious about humans. Wanted to know why they were different and spent alot of time cutting them up, trying to make something spirit like out of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T14:24:09-08:00","id":400841,"title":"","content":"What if Idigams are the remnants of the former humanity spirits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T14:43:58-08:00","id":400861,"title":"","content":"They come from well before humanity, so that would be a conundrum. Plus the constant change doesn't really fit humanity's domain. And the ones we've seen have Influences that aren't humanity.<br /> <br /> As always, it's something people might do for homebrew. I don't think it's their origin, though.<br /> <br /> It seems more like Galactus. They are the surviving spirits of a previous universe. Or perhaps just the concept of 'possibility' that has been narrowed down by reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-10-2015, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:09:13-08:00","id":400881,"title":"","content":"I would say they are Lesser Dephts's Spirits : spiritual entities who symbolize something that never had existed, have an evident uncomplet pattern and are mostly defined by what they are lacking.<br /> <br /> '","signature":"","edited":{"userid":343,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","user":"Suleri Drals","date":". 02-10-2015, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T02:23:07-08:00","id":401681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/400636-idigam-and-mankind?p=400861#post400861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They come from well before humanity, so that would be a conundrum. Plus the constant change doesn't really fit humanity's domain. And the ones we've seen have Influences that aren't humanity.<br /> <br /> As always, it's something people might do for homebrew. I don't think it's their origin, though.<br /> <br /> It seems more like Galactus. They are the surviving spirits of a previous universe. Or perhaps just the concept of 'possibility' that has been narrowed down by reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I don't think it's their origin either, but I think it fits more than you think.<br /> <br /> History and time in the NuWoD is far from neat and linear, so the &quot;preceding humanity&quot; is not as big a deterrent as it appears as first sight. What if Luna grew angry with humans and cut their spiritual reflections so damm violently it got retroactive?<br /> <br /> As for the constant change, I can not but see some similarities on how humankind manipulates nature, molding and changing it to suit their needs, and how the Idigam can do the same with Essence. Also, see how a Idigam either chooses its Influences and is shaped by them, or is changed and given Influences by his surroundings at the moment of coalescence. Just like humans start with no particular skill, but can choose wich ones to focus on and that changes them (becoming a doctor, or policeman, skill and abilities define humans and what they are) or are also shaped by the circumstances of its surroundings (if you live in a place dominated by gangs you have more chances to end up in one, and get a related set of skills).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T06:24:28-08:00","id":404427,"title":"","content":"Even for the spirits, humanity is a vastly important element of the World of Darkness. How the history of the Idigam interacts with that of humanity itself is something that the Idigam write-up of the new corebook does touch on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T02:03:21-08:00","id":405602,"title":"","content":"I hope that there will be Second Edition books for Skinchangers and Immortals because with Idigrams being part of the spirit hierarchy, I wonder if Skinchangers and Purified will be tied to certain Idigrams because they are spirit-bound. That would put an extra dimension to their lifestyles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T02:58:15-08:00","id":405622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/400636-idigam-and-mankind?p=400861#post400861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems more like Galactus. They are the surviving spirits of a previous universe. Or perhaps just the concept of 'possibility' that has been narrowed down by reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are the bastard shards of the Wyrd, Weaver, and Wyrm. When the old world finally collapsed under it's own weight, it's citizens were cast in the void beyond. Oblivion stood triumphant before devouring it's self, leaving all that couldn't be consumed to drift in the Abyssal blackness of the void. And drift they did. For time beyond time, eon beyond eon. Bits of their substance fading away. Strange complexities take shape. Morphing, changing, wanting, lusting. They are spat out worlds and summoned by lessor creatures. They forget themselves and in doing so, forget their nature.<br /> <br /> Until they are eventually spat out from this one. Either from the arcane mechanisms of a system who's reach is beyond space and time or perhaps the insane babbling of a half lucid god-spirit. They are thrown here. Stumbling into the light like deformed newborns. Old missions and directives echo dimly through their minds but oh so much has been forgotten and so much is not even relevant to the world they now inhabit. Now they twist without knowing, breaking while shaping. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T03:25:11-08:00","id":405635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/400636-idigam-and-mankind?p=405602#post405602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope that there will be Second Edition books for Skinchangers and Immortals because with Idigrams being part of the spirit hierarchy, I wonder if Skinchangers and Purified will be tied to certain Idigrams because they are spirit-bound. That would put an extra dimension to their lifestyles.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could certainly have Skinchangers and Purified as things that particular Idigam are creating, or that are traditions drawn from ancient pacts or discoveries related to the idigam in aeons past.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say that Idigam are part of the spirit hierarchy, however; they're more off to one side of it. The arrival of Idigam often fucks just as badly with the local spirit ecology as it does with everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T05:55:56-08:00","id":405713,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure it would be implied somewhere that Luna could have been an Idigam herself, she is a weird and changing being who breaks rules, ect....<br /> Moreover, Luna and the Idigam in Forsaken are pretty much the same that Luna and the Unshaped in Exalted, and it's implied that she could have been an Unshaped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T07:32:48-08:00","id":405777,"title":"","content":"Not so much 'could have been an Idigam' as much as 'is very similar in nature, except for the fact that she ultimately still works the way other non-Idigam work'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T08:17:42-08:00","id":405814,"title":"","content":"After all the physical moon is born from the collision of the proto-planet Theia and Earth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/400636-idigam-and-mankind?p=405777#post405777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not so much 'could have been an Idigam' as much as 'is very similar in nature, except for the fact that she ultimately still works the way other non-Idigam work'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe she have learned to &quot;congeal&quot; herself so much that she have lost her Idigam way of work and had gain a analog in the moon ? she has also a role as a representation of the Shadow itself that is abnormal for a spirit. (She is the Queen of the Shadow, she is somewhat the Spirit of spirits.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":343,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","user":"Suleri Drals","date":". 02-14-2015, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T07:49:39-08:00","id":406697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/400636-idigam-and-mankind?p=405777#post405777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not so much 'could have been an Idigam' as much as 'is very similar in nature, except for the fact that she ultimately still works the way other non-Idigam work'.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe the Idigam are her kids from a marriage before Father Wolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T09:53:51-08:00","id":406796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/400636-idigam-and-mankind?p=405814#post405814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all the physical moon is born from the collision of the proto-planet Theia and Earth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe she have learned to &amp;quot;congeal&amp;quot; herself so much that she have lost her Idigam way of work and had gain a analog in the moon ? she has also a role as a representation of the Shadow itself that is abnormal for a spirit. (She is the Queen of the Shadow, she is somewhat the Spirit of spirits.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Idigam can coalesce and accept a permanent Ban - it makes them much more powerful, but it also makes them much more like a normal spirit. That's how they eventually beat Gurdilag. Could be that Luna Coalesced as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T10:14:24-08:00","id":406810,"title":"","content":"Correlation doesn't implies causation. Luna represents something: the Moon. The fact that she changes every night is based on it's mundane analogue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T10:20:00-08:00","id":406814,"title":"","content":"What about every other moon in the universe? Are they all idigam too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T10:33:23-08:00","id":406820,"title":"","content":"The question that needs to be asked first is &quot;do other moons act as Luna does?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T12:39:55-08:00","id":406889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/400636-idigam-and-mankind?p=406820#post406820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question that needs to be asked first is &amp;quot;do other moons act as Luna does?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Like astrophysically or metaphysically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T12:41:28-08:00","id":406890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/400636-idigam-and-mankind?p=406810#post406810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correlation doesn't implies causation. Luna represents something: the Moon. The fact that she changes every night is based on it's mundane analogue.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be a result of her coalescence though, if that's the kind of story you want to tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}